$$
\begin{aligned}
-1&\le \cos\left(-4x+\pi\right)\le 1
\end{aligned}
$$

Multiply by $-4$, reversing both inequalities. Then subtract $1$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
4&\ge -4\cos\left(-4x+\pi\right)\ge -4 \\3&\ge -4\cos\left(-4x+\pi\right)-1\ge -5 \\-5&\le f(x)\le 3
\end{aligned}
$$

Both endpoint values and every value between them are attained. Therefore, the range is $f(x)\in[-5,3]$.
